WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:04.840
Leah: As well as barriers to seeking
a diagnosis, some children and young

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.000
people may be reluctant to have a
diagnosis or any medical intervention

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:11.620
because of a range of different concerns.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.350
Let’s have a look at
some of those concerns.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.329
Rhiannon: There can be stigma associated
with receiving a mental health diagnoses,

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.080
and although this is lessening, as
young people are more open to exploring

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.569
mental health issues, there are
still those that would discriminate.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:31.290
Being labelled with a mental
health diagnosis, might impact on

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.790
how others, including family and
friends may interact with someone.

00:00:38.519 --> 00:00:42.059
Leah: Parents of a child or young
person, may become overly cautious

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.810
around a mental health label.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.169
This may unintentionally reinforce
the underlying problem, such

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:51.379
as not encouraging an anxious
child to try new things.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.090
For some a diagnosis can put an
emphasis on the problem being a part

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.190
of the child or young person and
maybe less likely to take into account

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:04.750
other external factors such as the
family dynamic and peer interactions.

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:10.100
Rhiannon: Some diagnoses are more helpful
than others, diagnoses of depression

00:01:10.389 --> 00:01:16.220
or obsessive-compulsive disorder [OCD]
can validate suffering, however some

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:21.170
individuals might be sceptical of any
diagnostic label placed on them, as

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:25.839
they may feel dismissed by others who
choose to use their diagnosis as a way

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.039
of explaining away their valid emotions.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.960
More severe diagnoses, such
as schizophrenia or borderline

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.990
personality disorder, can be used
to damage the credibility of the

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.919
sufferer, silencing their voice.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.359
Leah: Some families of children and
young people, may fear that a diagnosis

00:01:46.389 --> 00:01:50.220
will impact on their progression or
opportunities, such as not being able

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:54.230
to handle University or not being
able to have that job role they want,

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.970
due to their mental health issues.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.089
This could then impact their
ambition for their future.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:04.449
They may fear that the information held
about their diagnoses, may be available

00:02:04.449 --> 00:02:06.810
to others, including potential employers.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.859
They may wish to keep parts of their
life, or their mental health issues

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.120
private, however this is not the
case due to data protection laws.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:19.900
Rhiannon: They may be concerned about
being put into a box, based solely on

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:24.079
their symptoms, rather than looking at
the cause of the symptoms themselves.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:29.830
Sometimes it is an experience of trauma,
abuse, or neglect that brings on the

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.760
symptoms of mental health conditions.

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:35.389
They may not wish to address
these issues and feel that medical

00:02:35.389 --> 00:02:39.209
intervention, may cause things that
have been suppressed to resurface.

00:02:40.639 --> 00:02:44.519
Leah: How a diagnosis is received
is also mediated by the individual’s

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.390
life experiences and culture.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:51.140
If the diagnosis is placed upon the
patient with no space for the individual’s

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.360
thoughts, queries, or concerns, then
it is likely that the individual

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.550
will reject the diagnosis and rebel
against any potential treatment plans.

